# Fizzleworth-witchguard.lic
# Rift hazards: while a witch, a warlock, a caedera (the Rift's worm), a csetairi or a worm is alive in the room, set
# bigshot's own global flee flag so bigshot leaves the room through its normal flee path -- whatever
# profile happens to be loaded.
#
# Why: 11/04 17:02 a Vvrael witch's ground spell took Fizzleworth to 29% and 17:17 she killed him. The
# profile's `always_flee_from: vvrael witch` never matched (bigshot compares that list to a creature's
# noun or full name EXACTLY: the game says "a steadfast Vvrael witch", noun "witch"), and the corrected
# value only applies after `;bigshot profile load`, which is easy to miss. This script needs neither.
#
# bigshot reads $bigshot_flee at the top of should_flee? and clears it after each move, so setting it
# every poll while the hazard is here keeps it fleeing, room after room, until none is left.
# Black voids too (11/04 evening): "The air begins to thin rapidly ... Air is sucked away from you!" is a
# swirling black void's attack, and bigshot's own flee_voids didn't get it out of the room (log: it fought
# in rooms listing "a swirling black void" for 9+ s). Voids can show up as room objects or as creatures,
# so every list is checked.
#
# 11/04 evening: caedera ("explodes from the ground"; Lich files it as a Worm, so the "worm" players warned
# about) and csetairi (L81) added -- Scott called them dangerous. The bare word "worm" would NOT have
# matched a caedera, whose name and noun are both "caedera". Vvrael warlocks (L84) too -- Scott: "like the witches".
#
# Started by Fizzleworth-prep in `sever` (Rift) mode and stopped by it in any other mode.
# It keeps its old code until restarted: ;kill Fizzleworth-witchguard, then ;Fizzleworth-witchguard.
# Run it by hand too: ;Fizzleworth-witchguard      Stop: ;kill Fizzleworth-witchguard

module WitchGuard
  module_function

  POLL   = 0.3
  HAZARD = /\b(?:witch|warlock|worm|caedera|csetairi)\b/i   # noun or name; "Vvrael witch", "Vvrael warlock", "caedera", "csetairi"
  VOID   = /black void/i                                    # "a swirling black void"

  def hazard_here
    Array(GameObj.npcs).find do |n|
      n && n.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ && (n.noun.to_s =~ HAZARD || n.name.to_s =~ HAZARD)
    end
  end

  # A black void in the room, wherever Lich filed it (room objects, room description, creatures).
  def void_here
    (Array(GameObj.loot) + Array(GameObj.room_desc) + Array(GameObj.npcs)).find do |o|
      o && o.name.to_s =~ VOID && o.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/
    end
  rescue StandardError
    nil
  end

  def run
    echo "[witchguard] on: making bigshot flee from witches, warlocks, caedera, csetairi, worms and black voids."
    seen = nil
    loop do
      begin
        hazard = hazard_here || void_here
        if hazard
          $bigshot_flee = true
          if seen != hazard.id
            echo "[witchguard] #{hazard.name} here -- telling bigshot to flee."
            seen = hazard.id
          end
        else
          seen = nil
        end
      rescue StandardError => e
        echo "[witchguard] error: #{e.class} #{e.message}"
        sleep 2
      end
      sleep POLL
    end
  end
end

WitchGuard.run
